# THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC.
#
# Everything this tool produces is sensitive: camera GPS positions are the
# physical locations of your cameras, and the photos are what they saw. None of
# it belongs in a public repo, so the sync output is excluded wholesale rather
# than file by file — a rule that only listed today's filenames would quietly
# stop covering a new one.
spypoint-data/
*/spypoint-data/

# Belt and braces: even if output lands somewhere unexpected, or a run is
# pointed elsewhere with --out, these patterns still catch it.
cameras.raw.json
cameras.csv
photos.jsonl
dashboard.html
trailcam.db
trailcam.db-wal
trailcam.db-shm
photos/
*.jpg
*.jpeg

# Credentials. sync.cmd is the Task Scheduler wrapper, which holds the SpyPoint
# password in plain text by necessity.
sync.cmd
sync.sh
.env
.env.*
# Written by Start-TrailCam.ps1. DPAPI-encrypted to one Windows account, but a
# credential file all the same and never belongs in a public repo.
.credentials.xml

# Node / editor noise
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# Downloaded collar datasets — CC0, but too big for the repo (see collar-data/README.md)
collar-data/*
!collar-data/README.md
